1
00:00:02,336 --> 00:00:03,337
Huh?

2
00:00:07,382 --> 00:00:09,800
You kids okay? No one's hit?

3
00:00:09,801 --> 00:00:12,262
Draken! Yeah, we're okay.

4
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:16,934
{\an8}[whimpers]

5
00:00:20,103 --> 00:00:24,233
Draken, I had a vision
that Senju died here protecting me.

6
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:27,486
But she's... she's still alive.

7
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:31,114
We avoided something terrible today.

8
00:00:31,782 --> 00:00:33,033
I guess so.

9
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:35,076
[chuckles]

10
00:00:35,077 --> 00:00:36,619
Well, good then.

11
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:38,455
[Senju] Hey, we gotta go.

12
00:00:39,164 --> 00:00:40,624
Oh, yeah, let's go.

13
00:00:42,709 --> 00:00:44,585
Draken, you coming?

14
00:00:44,586 --> 00:00:46,380
- [Ken] Takemichi...
- Huh?

15
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:48,924
[Ken] Tell Mikey something for me.

16
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:55,514
[labored]
Tell him I'm sick of worrying about him.

17
00:00:58,558 --> 00:01:00,435
- [body splashes]
- [gasps]

18
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:05,315
No can do. This is far as I go.

19
00:01:07,985 --> 00:01:10,529
[♪ theme song playing]

20
00:02:38,033 --> 00:02:39,326
{\an8}TRINITY LAND

21
00:02:43,747 --> 00:02:46,625
{\an8}[rain pattering]

22
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:51,463
{\an8}[silence]

23
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:56,593
{\an8}[Ken] <i>I can't hear.</i>

24
00:02:57,594 --> 00:02:59,011
[chuckles]

25
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:00,889
<i>Can't move my hands either.</i>

26
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:05,602
<i>The sky is... dark.</i>

27
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:08,897
[sound fades in]

28
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:11,858
[breathing heavily]

29
00:03:12,442 --> 00:03:14,652
Draken, when did you...

30
00:03:14,653 --> 00:03:18,739
I'll call an ambulance. Stay here
and keep talking to him, Hanagaki.

31
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:20,450
Make sure he stays awake, okay?

32
00:03:21,952 --> 00:03:23,619
[Takemichi] Draken!

33
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:25,371
Draken, hey!

34
00:03:25,372 --> 00:03:26,872
Can you hear me?

35
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:28,499
Say something!

36
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,794
[breathing heavily]

37
00:03:32,087 --> 00:03:34,047
Why are you looking at me like that?

38
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:36,633
Never seen a guy die before?

39
00:03:37,551 --> 00:03:39,260
We got an ambulance on the way.

40
00:03:39,261 --> 00:03:40,971
[weeping]

41
00:03:42,514 --> 00:03:45,809
You'll be just fine, Draken.
Got nothing to worry about, okay?

42
00:03:53,817 --> 00:03:55,110
Okay.

43
00:04:00,157 --> 00:04:01,241
So this is...

44
00:04:03,743 --> 00:04:05,704
what it's like to die.

45
00:04:08,582 --> 00:04:11,625
[Takemichi] No way, man!
What are you talking about?

46
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:14,713
You're gonna be totally fine by tomorrow.
You'll see.

47
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:16,882
You'll see.

48
00:04:18,175 --> 00:04:20,135
You're Draken. You can't.

49
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:22,137
[groans]

50
00:04:23,597 --> 00:04:25,348
Takemitchy...

51
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:29,436
You shouldn't blame yourself.

52
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:32,647
[whimpering]

53
00:04:33,315 --> 00:04:36,818
[Ken] This didn't happen
because you came back to the past.

54
00:04:46,077 --> 00:04:48,163
You're the one who gave me this life.

55
00:04:49,206 --> 00:04:51,416
It's only fitting that I give it back.

56
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:56,755
Hey, come on.

57
00:04:57,923 --> 00:04:59,466
You understand me?

58
00:05:01,718 --> 00:05:02,719
Yeah.

59
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:20,320
[raspy breathing]

60
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:23,949
Back when I was in elementary school,

61
00:05:24,825 --> 00:05:27,535
I lost every fight I was ever in.

62
00:05:27,536 --> 00:05:28,537
Huh?

63
00:05:29,538 --> 00:05:32,666
I only ever tried to pick fights
with the older kids.

64
00:05:35,085 --> 00:05:37,045
And they'd lay me out flat.

65
00:05:37,796 --> 00:05:39,714
Sprawled out just like this.

66
00:05:40,549 --> 00:05:43,260
But as I laid there
and looked up at the sky...

67
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:50,100
somehow, it would all just melt away,

68
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:52,269
and I'd feel...

69
00:05:56,815 --> 00:05:59,359
I hear ya. I get it.

70
00:06:01,027 --> 00:06:03,196
Mikey's never seen this sky.

71
00:06:03,989 --> 00:06:05,240
Doesn't know it.

72
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:07,367
What?

73
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:13,874
Never having lost before,
that's a tricky thing.

74
00:06:16,418 --> 00:06:17,836
[Takemichi crying]

75
00:06:18,879 --> 00:06:20,337
Takemitchy.

76
00:06:20,338 --> 00:06:22,047
[Takemichi] Huh?

77
00:06:22,048 --> 00:06:26,636
I really do love that kid. You know that?

78
00:06:28,054 --> 00:06:29,221
{\an8}FIRST GENERATION
TOKYO MANJI GANG

79
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:32,975
{\an8}<i>He puts the weight of the world
on his shoulders...</i>

80
00:06:32,976 --> 00:06:36,229
{\an8}<i>but he always pulls through somehow.</i>

81
00:06:39,357 --> 00:06:41,443
And just a kid underneath it all.

82
00:06:44,821 --> 00:06:47,073
I was with him... [groans]

83
00:06:47,699 --> 00:06:50,576
...every step of the way.

84
00:06:50,577 --> 00:06:53,329
Which is why... [coughs]

85
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:58,168
Which is why I wanted to be the one
to fix this for him.

86
00:06:59,419 --> 00:07:00,462
[Takemichi] Draken...

87
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:05,258
Okay, Takemitchy.

88
00:07:07,427 --> 00:07:10,638
Can I say just one more lame thing?

89
00:07:10,639 --> 00:07:12,057
Is that cool?

90
00:07:13,016 --> 00:07:14,059
[Takemichi] Yes.

91
00:07:19,439 --> 00:07:21,524
Please take care of him for me.

92
00:07:28,031 --> 00:07:29,157
[Takemichi] I will!

93
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:36,538
Responsive to verbal stimulus.

94
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:39,500
[medic] Hang in there.
We're gonna load you into the ambulance.

95
00:07:39,501 --> 00:07:40,960
You're all right, man!

96
00:07:42,754 --> 00:07:44,381
[raspy breathing]

97
00:07:46,716 --> 00:07:48,093
{\an8}[no audible dialogue]

98
00:07:50,679 --> 00:07:53,264
[breathing slows]

99
00:07:56,851 --> 00:08:00,604
JANUARY 1, 2005
FIRST SUNRISE RUN

100
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:02,649
[motorcycle engines roaring]

101
00:08:03,316 --> 00:08:06,778
- [Hakkai] To the sea!
- [Nahoya] Happy New Year!

102
00:08:08,822 --> 00:08:13,158
Baji, thought Harajuku was Olympus turf.
What happened?

103
00:08:13,159 --> 00:08:14,660
It was.

104
00:08:14,661 --> 00:08:18,873
What, you didn't hear? First Division
crushed those small fries all on our own.

105
00:08:19,374 --> 00:08:21,917
- Didn't we, Chifuyu?
- Yes, sir!

106
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:23,836
Anybody who crosses Baji

107
00:08:23,837 --> 00:08:27,381
is gonna get stripped down
and beaten within an inch of their life.

108
00:08:27,382 --> 00:08:31,468
Yeah, well, taking Baji's orders too far
is nothing to shoot your mouth off about.

109
00:08:31,469 --> 00:08:32,804
Better watch yourself.

110
00:08:33,596 --> 00:08:35,264
And Nitoro in Akasaka?

111
00:08:35,265 --> 00:08:37,349
Oh, we took them out ages ago.

112
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:38,767
Angry will tell ya.

113
00:08:38,768 --> 00:08:42,688
You wanna talk about taking it too far,
I spent the whole time holding him back.

114
00:08:42,689 --> 00:08:45,774
Toman's taking off like a rocket. Whoo!

115
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:48,444
We got the baddest boss in the business
is why.

116
00:08:48,445 --> 00:08:51,947
Mikey's been on fire lately.
Let him burn, I say.

117
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:54,575
You gotta. No dousing that inferno.

118
00:08:54,576 --> 00:08:57,077
The base of Tokyo Manji Gang.

119
00:08:57,078 --> 00:08:59,122
The Invincible Mikey.

120
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:05,586
I hope nothing's wrong though.
He's been kinda distant recently.

121
00:09:05,587 --> 00:09:06,671
Yeah, I suppose.

122
00:09:07,422 --> 00:09:09,340
Still got me, closer than ever.

123
00:09:11,051 --> 00:09:14,011
Hey, we'll never make sunrise like this!

124
00:09:14,012 --> 00:09:15,513
Hit the gas!

125
00:09:17,891 --> 00:09:20,726
- [waves lapping]
- [Pah-chin laughs] We finally made it!

126
00:09:20,727 --> 00:09:22,561
[Ken] Wow! The stars are poppin'!

127
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:25,564
[Keisuke shivers]
I forgot how cold it is in Kujūkuri!

128
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:27,941
Chifuyu, Hakkai,
go to the convenience store

129
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:29,902
and get me something hot
before I freeze to death!

130
00:09:29,903 --> 00:09:31,236
- [Chifuyu] Yes, sir!
- [Hakkai] Got it!

131
00:09:31,237 --> 00:09:34,908
[Takashi] Wait. It's only 4:00 a.m.
What time is sunrise?

132
00:09:39,537 --> 00:09:41,538
[Nahoya] This is just brutal.

133
00:09:41,539 --> 00:09:43,332
[Pah-chin] Will to live, man!

134
00:09:43,333 --> 00:09:46,418
- [Ken] Well, run! Start running.
- [Takashi] Are you kidding me?

135
00:09:46,419 --> 00:09:49,213
[Peh-yan] Wait,
why isn't the Fifth Division here?

136
00:09:49,214 --> 00:09:51,173
[Keisuke]
Mucho said driving out was a hassle.

137
00:09:51,174 --> 00:09:53,926
[Nahoya]
That cat can be a real turd sometimes.

138
00:09:53,927 --> 00:09:55,427
[Souya] Mind your language!

139
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:58,180
Sleep-running, Pah-chin? Wake up already.

140
00:09:58,181 --> 00:10:00,225
[Pah-chin] I'm awake! I'm awake!

141
00:10:02,936 --> 00:10:05,605
[Chifuyu] Hey, guys, we got the stuff!

142
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:08,524
[Chifuyu]
What the hell are they doing out there?

143
00:10:08,525 --> 00:10:10,443
[Hakkai]
They've got a lot of energy, don't they?

144
00:10:15,115 --> 00:10:17,367
- [panting]
- I shouldn't have done that.

145
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:22,204
Look, the sun's finally coming up.

146
00:10:22,205 --> 00:10:23,289
Huh?

147
00:10:31,339 --> 00:10:33,716
TOKYO MANJI GANG

148
00:10:48,398 --> 00:10:49,607
[chuckles]

149
00:10:51,192 --> 00:10:52,485
And there she is.

150
00:10:53,194 --> 00:10:55,863
Yeah! First sunrise of the year!

151
00:10:55,864 --> 00:10:58,658
- Bro, wake up! You're missing it.
- [Pah-chin] I am awake, you douchebag!

152
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:04,538
FIRST GENERATION VICE-LEADER
FIRST GENERATION LEADER

153
00:11:04,539 --> 00:11:05,748
[Mikey] Kenny...

154
00:11:09,419 --> 00:11:11,671
It's ours. All of it.

155
00:11:12,505 --> 00:11:17,135
Yeah. By year's end,
we'll conquer Japan. [chuckles]

156
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:19,846
[laughter echoes]

157
00:11:49,626 --> 00:11:51,419
I'll be there real soon...

158
00:11:52,212 --> 00:11:53,379
Emma.

159
00:11:57,550 --> 00:11:59,093
[giggling]

160
00:12:06,392 --> 00:12:09,103
- [Emma giggling]
- [Ken chuckling]

161
00:12:12,482 --> 00:12:13,774
No, please! You can't go yet!

162
00:12:13,775 --> 00:12:16,735
He's gonna make it, right?
He's gonna be okay.

163
00:12:16,736 --> 00:12:18,821
- [monitor flatlining]
- [gasps]

164
00:12:19,447 --> 00:12:20,615
[medic] I'm sorry.

165
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:22,616
We just lost him.

166
00:12:22,617 --> 00:12:24,494
[flatline continues]

167
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:26,496
[whimpers]

168
00:12:31,501 --> 00:12:33,544
[flatline continues]

169
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:37,257
[flatline fades out]

170
00:12:43,096 --> 00:12:45,264
[person grunting]

171
00:12:45,265 --> 00:12:48,225
{\an8}BLOSSOMS OF GLORY
ROKUHARA TANDAI

172
00:12:48,226 --> 00:12:50,852
[South] Now whose bright idea was it

173
00:12:50,853 --> 00:12:52,479
to shoot Draken?

174
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,898
Spit it out already!

175
00:12:54,565 --> 00:12:56,149
[blubbering]

176
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:59,194
[South] Who said you could go
and do a thing like that?

177
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:01,614
[stammers] We didn't mean to...

178
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:04,783
We were... Hanagaki.

179
00:13:04,784 --> 00:13:06,326
[thudding, crunching]

180
00:13:06,327 --> 00:13:07,786
[groaning]

181
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:10,872
These geniuses
used to be members of Toman.

182
00:13:10,873 --> 00:13:13,918
<i>Hanagaki's the one who sent them to juvie.</i>

183
00:13:14,502 --> 00:13:16,503
So when they got out, they looked him up

184
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:18,964
and found out
he's something of a big shot now.

185
00:13:18,965 --> 00:13:21,008
Thought they would go
exact their revenge on him.

186
00:13:21,009 --> 00:13:24,803
What gall.
All this over a middle school grudge.

187
00:13:24,804 --> 00:13:27,639
It's no small wonder
the boss is flying off the handle.

188
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,391
- Not quite.
- Hmm?

189
00:13:29,392 --> 00:13:31,351
I wouldn't call this off the handle.

190
00:13:31,352 --> 00:13:33,479
- [thudding]
- [person whimpering]

191
00:13:35,523 --> 00:13:37,025
[moaning]

192
00:13:37,859 --> 00:13:40,486
You fellas really went
and stepped in it, huh?

193
00:13:41,863 --> 00:13:43,573
- Hmm?
- [person groaning]

194
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:53,665
[gulping, grunting]

195
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:57,045
How lucky for me to find
there's still one bullet left.

196
00:13:59,589 --> 00:14:01,299
[whimpering]

197
00:14:16,647 --> 00:14:19,108
[walk signal beeping]

198
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:23,654
[beeping stops]

199
00:14:25,656 --> 00:14:26,740
[horn honking]

200
00:14:26,741 --> 00:14:30,243
PEDESTRIANS AND BICYCLES ONLY

201
00:14:30,244 --> 00:14:32,080
[horns honking]

202
00:14:51,307 --> 00:14:53,475
[door opens, closes]

203
00:14:53,476 --> 00:14:54,893
[footsteps approaching]

204
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:57,980
[Takeomi] Damn it, Senju!
I'm hearing that Draken was killed.

205
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:01,191
What the hell happened
to you guys out there?

206
00:15:01,192 --> 00:15:02,776
[Wakasa] The guy who pulled the trigger

207
00:15:02,777 --> 00:15:05,655
was probably someone
from Rokuhara or Kanto Manji.

208
00:15:06,405 --> 00:15:08,866
Sounds like the bullet
was intended for Hanagaki,

209
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:11,576
but Ryuguji took took it for him instead.

210
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:13,078
[growls]

211
00:15:13,079 --> 00:15:14,413
[Senju] It's my fault.

212
00:15:15,540 --> 00:15:18,583
I asked Hanagaki
to go to the amusement park with me.

213
00:15:18,584 --> 00:15:20,001
If we hadn't gone...

214
00:15:20,002 --> 00:15:22,337
[Takeomi] Why would you even go
to a place like that?

215
00:15:22,338 --> 00:15:23,672
What possible business could--

216
00:15:23,673 --> 00:15:27,717
She's a kid. Don't need to give her
the third degree for acting like one.

217
00:15:27,718 --> 00:15:29,386
The third degree?

218
00:15:29,387 --> 00:15:31,555
She finally made a friend
her own age, dude.

219
00:15:31,556 --> 00:15:33,765
Someone she could talk to
about the stuff she won't tell--

220
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:36,476
So what?
What kind of sentimental shit is this?

221
00:15:36,477 --> 00:15:39,062
Do you understand that this crisis
has just struck a massive blow

222
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:41,481
- to the future of Brahman?
- Yeah, I get it.

223
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:44,568
Senju gets it. We all get it.
You're acting like--

224
00:15:44,569 --> 00:15:45,652
Waka.

225
00:15:45,653 --> 00:15:46,863
[Takeomi] Hmm?

226
00:15:50,616 --> 00:15:52,993
Go ahead. Finish what you were gonna say.

227
00:15:52,994 --> 00:15:54,287
Hmm.

228
00:15:55,496 --> 00:15:58,499
Is that why you've had such
a piss-poor attitude with our clients?

229
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:02,252
You can't hide behind being a kid now.

230
00:16:02,253 --> 00:16:06,006
I gave you every opportunity to smile
and nod and let me handle things.

231
00:16:06,007 --> 00:16:08,008
You're the one who wanted to step up.

232
00:16:08,009 --> 00:16:09,343
[sighs]

233
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:12,263
[Takeomi] Shit! What a frickin' mess.

234
00:16:14,849 --> 00:16:15,932
[exhales]

235
00:16:15,933 --> 00:16:17,226
Hmm?

236
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:20,438
[engines roaring in the distance]

237
00:16:22,732 --> 00:16:28,321
Gentlemen, we are gathered here tonight
for Draken's final requiem!

238
00:16:31,282 --> 00:16:32,408
[chuckles]

239
00:16:34,952 --> 00:16:37,413
One of my guys took responsibility.

240
00:16:37,914 --> 00:16:40,541
So I figured we'd better get out here
and settle this.

241
00:16:42,335 --> 00:16:45,129
I'll give you all a moment
to assemble your troops.

242
00:16:45,922 --> 00:16:47,505
And then we begin!

243
00:16:47,506 --> 00:16:51,344
Armageddon,
the final war that will end all wars!

244
00:16:53,304 --> 00:16:56,306
Benkei, call everyone in. We gotta talk.

245
00:16:56,307 --> 00:16:57,308
Right.

246
00:16:58,226 --> 00:17:01,311
[Takeomi] Rokuhara Tandai falls tonight.

247
00:17:01,312 --> 00:17:02,855
- [Senju] No!
- Huh?

248
00:17:04,523 --> 00:17:05,774
Senju...

249
00:17:05,775 --> 00:17:07,984
We're not doing this. Not now.

250
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:10,111
No? Then when, Senju?

251
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:12,656
I don't know when, but not today!

252
00:17:12,657 --> 00:17:14,866
You would rather
we just back down tonight?

253
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:16,410
Draken died today!

254
00:17:18,204 --> 00:17:19,871
You need to listen hard.

255
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:21,915
This isn't a bunch of little boys
on the playground

256
00:17:21,916 --> 00:17:24,459
trying to find out
who's the toughest anymore.

257
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:25,836
People are dying.

258
00:17:27,546 --> 00:17:30,090
Doesn't matter what little fantasy world
you think we should live in.

259
00:17:30,091 --> 00:17:31,716
There's no backing down.

260
00:17:31,717 --> 00:17:34,302
They kill one of ours,
so that means we have to kill them back?

261
00:17:34,303 --> 00:17:37,931
Yes. That is how this works.
They hurt you, you put them down.

262
00:17:37,932 --> 00:17:40,267
If we falter now, Brahman is finished.

263
00:17:40,268 --> 00:17:43,145
And I don't know about you,
but I don't want that to happen.

264
00:17:45,231 --> 00:17:46,357
[sighs]

265
00:17:51,696 --> 00:17:53,238
Hmm?

266
00:17:53,239 --> 00:17:54,824
Hey, Senju!

267
00:17:58,995 --> 00:17:59,996
Listen.

268
00:18:15,094 --> 00:18:17,887
Do me a favor
and let's do this some other time.

269
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:20,016
[both grunting]

270
00:18:20,725 --> 00:18:21,892
[Senju gasps]

271
00:18:26,939 --> 00:18:30,609
Unrivaled Senju,
why don't we go one-on-one?

272
00:18:30,610 --> 00:18:33,195
[breathing heavily] That's fine.

273
00:18:35,364 --> 00:18:37,033
But not today, please.

274
00:18:37,867 --> 00:18:41,621
It's all my fault.
He should still be here.

275
00:18:42,997 --> 00:18:44,372
- [laughing]
- [blow landing]

276
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:46,042
- [grunts]
- [all gasp]

277
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:48,460
It's all my fault.

278
00:18:48,461 --> 00:18:50,545
It's my rotten luck.

279
00:18:50,546 --> 00:18:52,964
[both grunting]

280
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:54,842
- [gasps]
- [Senju] Stay back, Takeomi!

281
00:18:56,552 --> 00:18:58,346
[gasping]

282
00:19:10,524 --> 00:19:13,735
[Keizo] I won't say
you can't hit a woman who won't fight,

283
00:19:13,736 --> 00:19:16,780
because Senju is our boss, after all.

284
00:19:16,781 --> 00:19:19,867
But this isn't how you wanted this to go,
is it?

285
00:19:20,368 --> 00:19:21,786
[growls]

286
00:19:29,627 --> 00:19:31,087
[South] You have one night.

287
00:19:33,923 --> 00:19:36,050
[motorcycle engines revving]

288
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:46,394
[breathes shakily]

289
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:59,072
NEWSPAPER

290
00:19:59,073 --> 00:20:01,074
[elevator dings, door opens]

291
00:20:01,075 --> 00:20:02,576
Hey there. Welcome in.

292
00:20:08,916 --> 00:20:10,167
Oh, it's you.

293
00:20:14,088 --> 00:20:16,172
[no audible dialogue]

294
00:20:16,173 --> 00:20:18,175
[♪ melancholy music plays]

295
00:20:45,286 --> 00:20:47,413
NOW RECRUITING PARTICIPANTS
MODEL AUDITION APPLICATION

296
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:04,763
[no audible dialogue]

297
00:21:04,764 --> 00:21:07,641
GET CERTIFIED

298
00:21:20,196 --> 00:21:23,031
{\an8}CAT ENCYCLOPEDIA
PET SHOP PALME MATSUNO

299
00:21:23,032 --> 00:21:26,702
FIRST GENERATION TOKYO MANJI

300
00:21:57,149 --> 00:22:00,319
Ken Ryuguji has just died.

301
00:22:01,362 --> 00:22:02,822
[music fades]

302
00:22:04,073 --> 00:22:05,407
[breathes shakily]

303
00:22:08,577 --> 00:22:09,620
I see.

304
00:22:11,038 --> 00:22:13,457
[♪ theme music playing]

305
00:23:41,003 --> 00:23:42,086
FAIRY TALE REVENGERS - PETIT

306
00:23:42,087 --> 00:23:43,088
#8
"SNOW WHITE WANTS TO BE FRIENDS"

307
00:23:44,006 --> 00:23:47,342
[Chifuyu] <i>This is so awkward.
What am I supposed to talk about?</i>

308
00:23:47,343 --> 00:23:49,594
<i>The queen is finally
coming out of her room again.</i>

309
00:23:49,595 --> 00:23:52,013
<i>I can't be the one
to bore her back inside.</i>

310
00:23:52,014 --> 00:23:53,890
- Hmm?
- [Chifuyu] A cat?

311
00:23:53,891 --> 00:23:55,224
- [meows]
- [gasps]

312
00:23:55,225 --> 00:23:57,268
[Chifuyu] My queen, do you like cats?

313
00:23:57,269 --> 00:24:00,188
Pardon me,
did anyone see a cat come through here?

314
00:24:00,189 --> 00:24:02,732
- Prince, you mean this cat?
- [gasps]

315
00:24:02,733 --> 00:24:04,943
I knew you were around here somewhere.

316
00:24:04,944 --> 00:24:07,362
Many thanks.
I'll take him home right away.

317
00:24:07,363 --> 00:24:10,990
[Chifuyu] <i>Oh, no. This is bad.
The queen's about to cry!</i>

318
00:24:10,991 --> 00:24:12,867
[whimpering]

319
00:24:12,868 --> 00:24:15,787
Good prince, might I implore you
to leave the cat with us?

320
00:24:15,788 --> 00:24:19,916
What? No, you idiot! He's my cat.
What's the matter with you?

321
00:24:19,917 --> 00:24:22,085
Hand over the cat right now!

322
00:24:22,086 --> 00:24:23,711
- Hmm?
- [meows]

323
00:24:23,712 --> 00:24:24,837
{\an8}- [queen giggles]
- [grunting]

324
00:24:24,838 --> 00:24:25,922
{\an8}- Let me go!
- [grunting]

325
00:24:25,923 --> 00:24:26,924
{\an8}TO BE CONTINUED

